# Generated data does not belong in git.
#
# It was committed anyway — `git add -f` in daily-brief.yml overrode these
# rules — until 2026-08-24. That put 948 MB (96% of the tracked tree) of
# regenerated artifacts into a 1.36 GB public repository growing ~35 MB/day,
# and made four workflows contend on one branch through an 8-attempt
# `git rebase -X theirs` loop.
#
# Durable storage is now a GitHub Release per day (`data-YYYY-MM-DD`), written
# and read by worldscope/blobsync.py. dist/ needs no storage at all: it is
# regenerated every run and reaches Pages via upload-pages-artifact, which
# never reads git.
#
# History still contains these paths; nothing was rewritten. blobsync's
# restore path can seed itself from that history if no release exists yet.
lake/
dist/
data/store.sqlite
data/store.sqlite-wal
data/store.sqlite-shm

# blobsync staging
.blobsync/

# Tailwind build artifacts
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.tailwindcss-cache/

